"""REV. 3 - 6m x 6m x 6m Cube - Structural Model (single-window app).

Sidebar (left) : compact dropdowns — Units, Apply-to group, Material,
        Section — plus Save xlsx+png. Changing a dropdown instantly
        redraws the viewer; Save rewrites the workbook + PNG.
Viewer (right) : dominant 3D frame (beams, columns, nodes, pinned
        supports at nodes 1-4, global X/Y/Z triad, local lx/ly/lz
        axes, M1-M12 labels, N# DOF tags, MZ/Mx release circles)
        + engineering data sheet (Geometry, Global Axes, Supports,
        Nodal DOF, Member End Releases, Beta Angles, Local Axes,
        Materials + Sections).

Model (same as REV2 / cubere1_risa): X/Z lateral, Y vertical,
N1 origin, N1-N4 PINNED, M1-M8 Mx+Mz released, columns M9-M12
beta 90 deg.

REV3 adds (per Revit 3 Solver Update prompt, architecture-first):
  - Centralized Unit System (Imperial + Standard Metric/SI,
    exact definitions from Units_Imperial_Metric.xlsx,
    convert-at-boundary, kN+m / E-kPa internal).
  - Material Library (A36 / A992 / Conc4000NW, per-member property,
    extensible to timber etc.).
  - Section Library (W10X22 / W12X26 / W8X18, per-member property,
    from aisc-shapes-database-v160-2.xlsx).
  - Validation (unknown material/section rejected, no silent
    unit mismatch) + dual-unit workbook sheets.

Outputs: REV3.xlsx (Nodes / Members / Supports / DOFs / LocalAxes
          + ModelInfo_Units / Materials / Sections)
         + REV3.png (two-panel viewer, 18 x 9.5, dpi 220)

Run:
    python REV3.py
"""

